Let's build out the battle system objects with proper C# structure. Based on your turn-based setup with multiple party members, magic, and skill items:

**Character.cs**  
- Return type: `Character`  
- Properties:  
  ```csharp
  public int Health { get; set; }
  public int Mana { get; set; }
  public int Strength { get; set; }
  public int Agility { get; set; }
  public List<Skill> Skills { get; set; } = new List<Skill>();
  public List<Item> Inventory { get; set; } = new List<Item>();
  public bool IsAlive => Health > 0;
  ```  
- Functions:  
  ```csharp
  public void TakeDamage(int damage) { Health -= damage; }
  public bool CastSpell(Skill spell) { 
      if (Mana >= spell.ManaCost) { 
          Mana -= spell.ManaCost; 
          return spell.ApplyEffect(this); 
      } 
      return false; 
  }
  public void UseItem(Item item) { 
      item.ApplyEffect(this); 
      Inventory.Remove(item); 
  }
  ```

**TurnManager.cs**  
- Return type: `Character`  
- Properties:  
  ```csharp
  private Queue<Character> turnQueue = new Queue<Character>();
  ```  
- Functions:  
  ```csharp
  public void AddToTurnQueue(Character character) { turnQueue.Enqueue(character); }
  public Character NextTurn() => turnQueue.Dequeue();
  public void ResetTurns(List<Character> party) { turnQueue.Clear(); party.ForEach(AddToTurnQueue); }
  ```

**Skill.cs**  
- Return type: `bool`  
- Properties:  
  ```csharp
  public string Name { get; }
  public int ManaCost { get; }
  public int Cooldown { get; set; }
  public bool IsReady => Cooldown <= 0;
  ```  
- Functions:  
  ```csharp
  public bool ApplyEffect(Character target) {
      // Example: Deal magic damage or apply debuff
      target.Health -= 10;
      return true;
  }
  public void UpdateCooldown() { 
      if (Cooldown > 0) Cooldown--; 
  }
  ```

**Item.cs**  
- Return type: `void`  
- Properties:  
  ```csharp
  public string Name { get; }
  public ItemType Type { get; }
  public int Quantity { get; set; }
  ```  
- Functions:  
  ```csharp
  public void ApplyEffect(Character user) {
      switch (Type) {
          case ItemType.Potion: user.Health += 20; break;
          case ItemType.MagicalAmmo: user.Mana += 15; break;
      }
  }
  ```

**Party.cs**  
- Return type: `List<Character>`  
- Properties:  
  ```csharp
  public List<Character> Members { get; } = new List<Character>();
  ```  
- Functions:  
  ```csharp
  public void AddMember(Character character) { 
      Members.Add(character); 
      // Auto-assign turn priority via Agility stat
      TurnManager.AddToTurnQueue(character); 
  }
  public List<Character> GetActiveMembers() => 
      Members.Where(c => c.IsAlive).ToList();
  ```

This setup supports your core needs:  
- `TurnManager` handles turn order with agility-based priority  
- Skills consume mana and have cooldowns  
- Items modify stats on use  
- Party management tracks alive members and auto-queues turns  

Want me to refine any object further? For example, we could add `MagicShield` or `CyberEnhancement` subclasses for skills/items.

